verses.tf_bn:
① **«اِذَا جَاۤءَكَ الْمُنٰفِقُوْنَ قَالُوْا نَشْهَدُ اِنَّكَ لَرَسُوْلُ اللّٰهِ»** — যখন কপট মুনাফিকরা আপনার দরবারে উপস্থিত হয়, তখন তারা মৌখিকভাবে জোর দিয়ে বলে: ‘আমরা কসম খেয়ে সাক্ষ্য দিচ্ছি যে আপনি নিশ্চয়ই আল্লাহর সত্য রাসুল!’
② **«وَاللّٰهُ یَعْلَمُ اِنَّكَ لَرَسُوْلُهٗ»** — অথচ আল্লাহ তাআলা অনাদিকাল থেকেই সম্যক জানেন যে আপনি অবশ্যই তাঁর মনোনীত মহান রাসুল—এতে কোনো সৃষ্টির মৌখিক সাক্ষ্যের আদৌ কোনো মুখাপেক্ষিতা নেই;
③ **«وَاللّٰهُ یَشْهَدُ اِنَّ الْمُنٰفِقِیْنَ لَكٰذِبُوْنَ»** — এবং আল্লাহ তাআলা স্বয়ং সাক্ষ্য দিচ্ছেন যে, এই মুনাফিকরা তাদের এই দাবিতে নিশ্চিতভাবেই ডাহা মিথ্যাবাদী! কারণ তাদের মুখের বচনের সাথে অন্তরের বিশ্বাসের কোনো মিল নেই; অন্তরে কুফর লুকিয়ে রেখে মুখে ঈমানের দাবি করাই হলো চরম মিথ্যাচার ও মুনাফেকি।

verses.tf_en:
① **«اِذَا جَاۤءَكَ الْمُنٰفِقُوْنَ قَالُوْا نَشْهَدُ اِنَّكَ لَرَسُوْلُ اللّٰهِ»** (When the hypocrites come in your presence (O dear Prophet Mohammed – peace and blessings be upon him) they say, “We testify that you surely are Allah’s Noble Messenger”;) — When the treacherous hypocrites enter into your august presence, O Holy Prophet ﷺ, they swear emphatic, solemn oaths with their tongues, declaring: 'We bear witness that you are indeed the true Messenger of Allah!';
② **«وَاللّٰهُ یَعْلَمُ اِنَّكَ لَرَسُوْلُهٗ»** (And Allah knows that you indeed are His Noble Messenger,) — Whereas Allah knows from all eternity with absolute certainty that you are indeed His chosen, Beloved Messenger—a divine reality needing no verification from the deceitful lips of hypocrites;
③ **«وَاللّٰهُ یَشْهَدُ اِنَّ الْمُنٰفِقِیْنَ لَكٰذِبُوْنَ»** (And Allah testifies that the hypocrites are indeed liars.) — And Allah Himself solemnly testifies that the hypocrites are utter liars in their declarations! For although their statement is true in itself, they are fraudulent liars in their intention and belief, professing with their lips what their treacherous hearts completely reject.

① **«وَاِذَا رَاَیْتَهُمْ تُعْجِبُكَ اَجْسَامُهُمْ وَاِنْ یَّقُوْلُوْا تَسْمَعْ لِقَوْلِهِمْ»** (And when you see them, their appearance would please you; and when they speak, you would listen carefully to their speech;) — When you look upon these hypocrites (such as 'Abdullah ibn Ubayy and his aristocratic cohort), you are outwardly impressed by their tall, handsome physiques and luxurious garments; and whenever they speak, their eloquent, polished rhetoric commands attention;
② **«كَاَنَّهُمْ خُشُبٌ مُّسَنَّدَةٌ»** (Like wooden blocks propped against the wall;) — Yet beneath this dazzling exterior, their souls are entirely hollow and devoid of genuine faith and intellect—standing spiritually inert like dried wooden logs propped against a wall, completely devoid of life, conscience, and moral substance!;
③ **«یَحْسَبُوْنَ كُلَّ صَیْحَةٍ عَلَیْهِمْ»** (They assume every cry to be against them;) — Stricken with chronic guilt and paranoid cowardice, whenever any sudden shout, military herald, or commotion arises in Madinah, they panic in terror, imagining that their treason has been exposed and that retribution has arrived to strike them down!;
④ **«هُمُ الْعَدُوُّ فَاحْذَرْهُمْ قٰتَلَهُمُ اللّٰهُ اَنّٰی یُؤْفَكُوْنَ»** (They are the enemy, so beware of them; may Allah slay them! Where are they reverting!) — They are the most lethal, insidious internal enemies of the Muslim community, so remain perpetually vigilant against them! May Allah destroy and confound them! To what depths of absurdity and perversity are they turning away from the luminous guidance of truth!
